    "role": "fabric-coordinator",
    "holders": [
      "user"
    ]
  },
  "contributors": [
    {
      "role": "python-dev",
      "merges": true,
      "note": "agent-fabric ADR-018 §5 rule 8: the code of the port of the fabric's bash to Python (ADR-040) and its Python tooling, on python-dev's own branch: since 2026-10-07 (`merges`) it opens, blind-reviews and merges its own pull request; fabric-coordinator distributes the merge. Definitions and the fence stay out: identities/, routing/, policies/ (but the allowlist the port shrinks), communication/ (but GZCoord's scripts and their tests, ADR-040's Wave 7), docs/adr/, memory/, .agent-fabric/, .github/; the guards and git.py, which they import; the lint and the suite runners; runtime/claude-code/ whole (the reviewer's agent file, the harness hooks and the settings that register them, the workspace prompt, bootstrap and install-agent-files); the review brief and its tooling; tests/leak-check.sh, which the suite runner sources; the role, routing and prompt code; the harness pins; the Python pin's installer, which runs as root on every host. Lint holds every entry to that list (CONTRIBUTOR_NEVER).",
